             ,HELPFUL HINTS

,FOR EVERYONE3 ,ONE THING IS THE SAME IN
  ALL THREE PICTURES3 WATER IS COMING UP
  FROM UNDER THE GROUND4 ,FROM A WELL BY
  PULLING UP A BUCKET1 FROM A HAND PUMP
  BY WORKING THE HANDLE1 AND FROM A TUBE
  WELL BY RUNNING A MOTOR4
,VISION3 ,IF THERE IS A HAND PUMP
  NEARBY1 HOLD ITS HANDLE1 MOVE IT UP
  AND DOWN AND LISTEN FOR THE WATER
  COMING4 ,STICK RAISED THINGS ONTO THE
  POSTER1 SUCH AS COTTON-WOOL DROPS AND
  A TAP MADE OF STRING4
,MOVEMENT3 ,EACH CHILD CAN HAVE A
  DIFFERENT JOB ON THE POSTER3 ONE GIVES
  IDEAS1 ONE CHOOSES PICTURES1 ONE PICKS
  THE COLOURS1 AND ONE STICKS THINGS ON4
  ,USE THICK MARKERS AND LARGE PICTURES4
,FOR TEACHERS3 ,MAKE MIXED GROUPS AND
  GIVE EACH CHILD A CLEAR ROLE SO THAT
  CHILDREN WITH DISABILITIES ARE NOT
  JUST ONLOOKERS4 ,PUT PICTURES OR
  SYMBOLS BESIDE THE WORDS ON THE POSTER
  SO THAT CHILDREN WHO CANNOT READ ALSO
  UNDERSTAND THE MESSAGE4

